    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0467" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.30/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-27T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                                1919—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 28—4
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Legation’s October 22, 10 a.m.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d425-f1"/></p>
                <p>President today asked me to ascertain if my Government would permit naval
                    commission come to Peru for the purpose of directing and reorganizing Peruvian
                    Navy.</p>
                <pb facs="0468" n="368" xml:id="pg368"/>
                <p>Also brought up the question of United States furnishing Marine police for
                    Callao. He stated that Foreign Office would, within short time, make official
                    request for above mentioned services.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
